# Concrete quadratic modules for the terminal orthogonal alternatives

The eight-point natural section retains its split quadratic coordinates. The
paired five-point cores retain both actions, their quadratic forms and the
factor swap, together with the isotropic rank obstruction.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, G.11.2(5),(12) and 12.8.13(5),(7).
-/
